    "note": "The common case: a bare due date's effective deadline is the END of the day, which sortDeadline computes as the next midnight (00:00), so the 120-minute lead fires at 22:00. With a 23:00 bedtime the quiet window opens at 22:00 (bedtime minus 60) and its comparison is strict, so 22:00 is outside it: this reminder passes the gate on its own and never touches the exemption, by exactly one minute. With a 22:00 bedtime the window would open at 21:00 and the same reminder would fire inside it, through the exemption."
